# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Terraform / OpenTofu ignores for the IAM/PAM lab.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Local provider plugins + module cache (regenerated by `init`).
**/.terraform/*

# State is SENSITIVE for an identity tenant - never commit it. It lives in the
# remote azurerm backend (see envs/dev/backend.tf).
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfstate.backup

# Real variable values (tenant ids, object ids, approver ids) - use the
# committed *.example as the template.
terraform.tfvars
*.auto.tfvars
secret.auto.tfvars

# Crash logs + plan artifacts.
crash.log
crash.*.log
*.tfplan

# The dependency lock files ARE committed for the seven roots (envs/dev,
# envs/bootstrap, aws, okta, k8s/platform, k8s/identity, k8s/aks-mapping; the
# last is plan-only, never applied): generated by HashiCorp
# Terraform 1.16.5 with `terraform providers lock -platform=linux_amd64
# -platform=darwin_arm64` (the first four also -platform=darwin_amd64) so CI
# runners and Macs verify the same provider hashes. The applied k8s roots keep LOCAL
# state (ephemeral kind cluster, no backend); *.tfstate above keeps it out.
# Child modules have no lock file (they inherit the root's), so a
# local `init` / `test` inside a module must not leave one to be published.
modules/*/.terraform.lock.hcl
